  "id": "COMPOUND:28197 - PROTEIN:5940",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Divaricataester C exerts its biological activity by targeting the CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase enzyme, which in turn is a target of multiple compounds, including 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide, Leosibirone B, and (1S,3E,4S,5S,6S)-4,5-dihydroxy-3-(3-methylbut-2-enylidene)-7-oxabicyclo[4.1.0]heptan-2-one. All these compounds ultimately target Carboxylesterase 2, indicating a potential pathway where Divaricataester C may interact with or inhibit Carboxylesterase 2 through a shared mechanism of action. The evidence suggests that the target enzyme is a critical mediator in the interaction between Divaricataester C and Carboxylesterase 2, possibly through a common pathway involving sialyltransferase activity. The integration of these paths highlights a possible dependency on the sialyltransferase enzyme, which may be a key component in the pharmacological profile of Divaricataester C.",
